{"story_id":"GH-66923-014","title":"Morning Sunrise","title_raw":"XIV.    “MORNING SUNRISE”","notes":"","language":"en","original_language":"und","country":"Ghana","country_code":"GH","culture_region":"西アフリカ(ゴールドコースト)","latitude":7.9,"longitude":-1.0,"location_precision":"culture_region","map_location_type":"source_culture_region","collector":"W. H. Barker; Cecilia Sinclair","translator":null,"publication_year":null,"year_evidence":"この電子版は版年を刻んでいない。註が 1914 年の統計に触れるので、それ以降の刊行である","book_id":"PG-66923","book_title":"West African Folk-Tales","source_provider":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/66923","source_title":"West African Folk-Tales","license_status":"PUBLIC_DOMAIN_US","license_name":"Public Domain (United States)","license_jurisdiction":"US","rights_evidence_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/66923","redistribution_allowed":true,"commercial_use":true,"derivative_use":true,"ml_processing_status":"reviewed","verification_date":"2026-09-08","word_count":276,"text":"A man in one of the villages had a very beautiful daughter. She was so\nlovely that people called her “Morning Sunrise.” Every young man who\nsaw her wanted to marry her. Three, in particular, were very anxious to\nhave her for their wife. Her father found it difficult to decide among\nthem. He determined to find out by a trick which of the three was most\nworthy of her.\n\nHe bade her lie down on her bed as if she were dead. He then sent the\nreport of her death to each of the three lovers, asking them to come\nand help him with her funeral.\n\nThe messenger came first to “Wise Man.” When he heard the message, he\nexclaimed, “What can this man mean? The girl is not my wife. I\ncertainly will not pay any money for her funeral.”\n\nThe messenger came next to the second man. His name was “Wit.” The\nlatter at once said, “Oh dear, no! I shall not pay any money for her\nfuneral expenses. Her father did not even let me know she was ill.” So\nhe refused to go.\n\n“Thinker,” the third young man—when he received the message—at once got\nready to start. “Certainly I must go and mourn for Morning Sunrise,”\nsaid he. “Had she lived, surely she would have been my wife.” So he\ntook money with him and set out for her home.\n\nWhen he reached it her father called out, “Morning Sunrise, Morning\nSunrise. Come here. This is your true husband.”\n\nThat very day the betrothal took place, and soon after the wedding\nfollowed. “Thinker” and his beautiful wife lived very happily together.","cluster":-1,"analysis":{"analysis_version":"1.0","embedding_model":"intfloat/multilingual-e5-small","themes":[{"label":"死","z":0.379,"strength":"弱","confidence":0.594,"method":"embedding"}],"motifs":[],"animals":[],"nature":[],"events":[{"position":0.0,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.091,"label":"Family","hits":1,"lift":10.25,"method":"count"},{"position":0.182,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.273,"label":"Death","hits":1,"lift":39.52,"method":"count"},{"position":0.364,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.455,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.545,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.636,"label":"Family","hits":1,"lift":10.25,"method":"count"},{"position":0.727,"label":"Trial","hits":1,"lift":26.54,"method":"count"},{"position":0.818,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.909,"label":"Departure","hits":1,"lift":129.97,"method":"count"},{"position":1.0,"label":"Marriage","hits":1,"lift":66.73,"method":"count"}],"tension":[{"position":0.0,"tension":0.5,"raw":-4.348,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.091,"tension":0.75,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.182,"tension":0.75,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.273,"tension":1.0,"raw":4.348,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.364,"tension":0.75,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.455,"tension":0.75,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexico